# App-domain device extras — Meizu MX6 (m95).
#
# /proc/ged, FACT (2026-08-14 census): every hardware-accelerated app process
# ioctl's the MTK GED node from its RenderThread —
#   avc: denied { ioctl } path="/proc/ged" ioctlcmd=6767
#        scontext=u:r:platform_app:s0 (x26) / u:r:priv_app:s0 (x6)
# Only { ioctl } was ever audited for app domains, which means the fd reaches
# the app without an open denial (most plausibly created by the GL stack
# before the app's first frame); open/read/getattr are granted with it anyway
# because a per-process GPU fd that cannot be reopened after the driver
# reinitialises is a latent breakage of exactly the kind permissive hides.
# untrusted_app is included deliberately: any GLES game hits the same path;
# isolated_app is not.
# No allowxperm — see the kernel xperm defect note in ioctl_xperms.te.
# 2026-09-24: superseded -- on Android 13 the command list is mandatory; it
# is granted for apps too in the bottom block of graphics.te.
allow { appdomain -isolated_app } proc_ged:file { getattr open read ioctl };
